se called Xiao Wang. So, we don't have information about incoming calls to Xiao Wang. Therefore, we can't infer that someone called Xiao Wang. So, option C might not be correct.\n\nOption D: Xiao Wang answered the phone from everyone in the administration department. Point 1 says Xiao Wang dialed everyone, which means he made outgoing calls. But it doesn't say that Xiao Wang received calls from everyone. So, we don't know if Xiao Wang was called by everyone. Therefore, option D might not be correct.\n\nWait, but let me double-check. Point 3 says that people who never answered calls from others also never called others. So, if Xiao Wang called everyone, including Xiao Li, Xiao Zhao, etc., then those people (like Xiao Li and Xiao Zhao) would have received calls. But since Xiao Zhao didn't call anyone else, it's possible that Xiao Zhao didn't answer any calls, including Xiao Li's. But for Xiao Wang, since he called everyone, including Xiao Li, Xiao Li must have received that call. But does that mean Xiao Li answered it? Not necessarily. So, we can't conclude that Xiao Wang was answered by everyone.\n\nWait, but the question is about who answered calls from others. So, if Xiao Wang called everyone, but we don't know if they answered. So, option D is about Xiao Wang answering everyone, which we can't infer.\n\nSo, going back, option A seems correct because Xiao Zhao didn't call anyone else, so he didn't answer any calls, including Xiao Li's.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A\n\nStep-by-step explanation:\n\n1. From point 3, since Xiao Zhao didn't call anyone else, he also didn't answer any calls.\n2. Therefore, Xiao Zhao never answered Xiao Li's call.\n3. This makes option A correct.\n\nAnswer: A",
