ontext suggests that because of the lack of respect for sovereignty, the world isn't peaceful. It implies that without all countries respecting each other, peace isn't achieved. So, D seems to align with the context.\n\nWait, but let me double-check. The context says that only when all countries respect sovereignty can the world be peaceful. Since some countries don't do this due to hegemony, the world isn't peaceful. So, D is the logical conclusion here.\n\nI think I'm confident that D is the correct answer because it directly relates to the problem described in the context.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: D\n\nThe context explains that world peace depends on all countries respecting each other's sovereignty. However, due to some countries' hegemonic attitudes, this isn't happening, leading to the conclusion that there's no real peace.\n\nThe correct option is: D",
