elopment of enterprises. While true, the context doesn't focus on why there are so many migrants but rather the problems that arise from them.\n\nOption C mentions low-quality floating populations not being good for development. That's true, but the context specifically ties it to the problem of unemployment and urbanization hindrance, so it's more about the effect than just the quality.\n\nOption D points out that unemployment is a crisis, which is a consequence mentioned, but the main point is about the effect on urbanization, not just the problem of unemployment itself.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the main point is that the floating population's negative impact is hindering urbanization, which is option A.\n</think>\n\nThe main point is that the increase of the floating population has a negative effect on the urbanization development of some areas.\n\nThe correct option is: A",
