k B is the correct answer because it directly addresses the negative impact of the parenting approach on the child's self-esteem.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B\n\nThe argument concludes that children's self-esteem will suffer if their parents uniformly praise their attempts to accomplish things regardless of their success or failure. This aligns with the context provided, which explains that excessive and consistent praise for both successes and failures can negatively impact a child's self-esteem.\n\nThe correct option is: B",
