which is illegal. But they did hit the brake, so maybe they avoided the accident. So the result was avoided because D took action. So this doesn't fit because the result was preventable.\n\nSo, putting it together, the correct answer should be option C because speeding is an illegal act, and the accident couldn't have been avoided even if C followed the law.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: C\n\nThe reasoning is that option C involves speeding, an illegal act, which led to an unavoidable accident. Even if C had driven legally, they might not have been able to avoid the accident, fitting the definition of obligatory alternative action.\n\nThe correct option is: C",
