sts, that might not be hospice care but rather aggressive treatment, which is more chemotherapy or other aggressive methods, not part of the standard hospice approach.\n\nSo the correct answer should be A because it's about extending life, which isn't the focus of hospice care.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A\n\nThe reasoning is that hospice care focuses on improving quality of life and comfort, not on extending the patient's life beyond what is medically possible. Option A involves aggressive treatment aimed at extending life, which doesn't align with the principles of hospice care.\n\nThe correct option is: A",
