hile economic and material factors are influencing marriages, they aren't the main or only factors. It also implies that parents are still considering these factors, which might indicate that people need to have a balanced view of marriage beyond just financial aspects. So D seems to align with the idea that a correct and positive attitude towards marriage is important.\n\nPutting it all together, the passage is highlighting that economic factors are influencing marriages, but they're not the only ones. It also suggests that parents are still considering these factors, which might mean that people need to have a proper understanding and attitude towards marriage. Therefore, the most likely conclusion is D.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: D) In order to have a good marriage, we should have a correct view of marriage and attitude towards marriage.",
