      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I'm trying to figure out which option best supports the experts' opinion that the decline of Easter Island's civilization isn't solely due to the felling of trees. Let me break this down step by step.\n\nFirst, the context says that Easter Island's civilization declined because people started cutting down palm trees, leading to loss of fertile soil and food shortages. But the experts argue that this might not be the whole story. So, the question is asking which of the options, if true, would support that idea.\n\nLooking at the options:\n\nOption A: Talks about cutting down palm trees around 1200 AD to build wooden boats and transport stone statues. This supports the original idea that tree cutting was a cause, so it doesn't support the experts' opinion. It actually does the opposite.\n\nOption B: Archaeological findings show that after the last tree was felled, people still lived and farming didn't decline. This directly contradicts the original report, which said that without trees, food was scarce. So this supports the experts because it shows that without trees, the society didn't necessarily decline, meaning tree cutting wasn't the main cause.\n\nOption C: Pollen analysis shows forests were destroyed starting in 800 AD, with less palm tree pollen over time. This supports the original report's claim because it shows the trees were being cut down, leading to soil loss. So it doesn't support the experts.\n\nOption D: Dutch colonists came in 1772 and enslaved locals, reducing population. This is more about population decline due to external factors, not directly about tree cutting causing soil loss. It doesn't directly address the experts' point about tree cutting not being the main cause.\n\nSo, the best option is B because it shows that even without trees, the society continued to exist and farm successfully, directly challenging the idea that tree cutting was the main cause of decline.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B\n\nThe reasoning is that option B directly contradicts the original report by showing that after the last tree was felled, the society still thrived, indicating that tree cutting wasn't the sole cause of decline. \n\nThe correct option is: B",
