tional system, legal point of view, art and even religious ideas must be explained on this basis.\n- This option talks about the various aspects that are influenced by the foundation of basic needs. It seems to tie together the foundation with the development of different aspects of society.\n\nNow, considering the context, it's explaining that human history's development (Marx's law) is based on people's basic needs first being met. This leads to the foundation for other aspects like national systems, law, art, and religion. So the gist is that the foundation of basic needs is crucial for the development of these other areas.\n\nOption B focuses on Marx's discovery but doesn't mention the broader implications. Option D connects the foundation to the various aspects, which seems to be the gist of the passage.\n\nI think the correct answer is D because it encapsulates the main idea that the foundation of basic needs is essential for explaining the development of other societal aspects, which is what the context is emphasizing.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: D\n\nThe passage emphasizes that the foundation of people satisfying their basic needs is crucial for the development of various societal aspects, such as national systems, law, art, and religion. This is the central theme, making option D the correct choice.\n\nThe correct option is: D",
