      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I'm trying to figure out which option supports the argument presented in the context. Let me break it down step by step.\n\nFirst, the context says that health officials are worried about rising alcohol-related deaths, attributing it to an increase in alcoholism. But they're missing something: alcoholism is now seen as a disease, not just a moral issue. So, more deaths are being reported because doctors are more likely to label them as alcohol-related.\n\nThe question is asking which option best supports this argument. So, I need to find the option that explains why more deaths are being identified as alcohol-related.\n\nLooking at the options:\n\nA) Talks about young people using alcohol at younger ages. That's more about the age of use, not why more deaths are being reported. So probably not the best fit.\n\nB) Says doctors recommend psychological counseling and support groups. That's about treatment, not about how doctors are identifying more deaths as alcohol-related. So maybe not directly relevant.\n\nC) States that in some places, disease susceptibility was viewed as a moral failing. This seems related because it's about changing attitudes where alcoholism was once seen as a moral issue, now a disease. But how does that directly tie into more deaths being reported? Maybe it supports the idea that the perception has changed, leading to more identification, but it's not directly about the increase in recognition.\n\nD) Says more doctors are trained to recognize alcohol effects. This directly relates to the argument because if more doctors are trained, they're more likely to diagnose and report alcohol-related deaths. That would explain the increase in reported deaths, supporting the argument.\n\nSo, D seems to be the best option because it's about increased training leading to more identification of alcohol-related deaths, which aligns with the context's reasoning.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: D\n\nThe reasoning is that option D directly supports the argument by stating that more physicians are trained to recognize the physical effects of alcoholism, which would lead to an increase in reported deaths as alcohol-related. This aligns with the context's explanation that changing attitudes and increased training contribute to the rise in reported cases.\n\nThe correct option is: D",
