t the question is asking which statement must be inconsistent, meaning it cannot be true based on the given facts. So, option B is impossible because A cannot equal C, given that A < B \u2264 C. Therefore, option B must be inconsistent.\n\nWait, but let me double-check. If A < B \u2264 C, then A is definitely less than C, so A cannot be equal to C. Therefore, option B is impossible, so it must be inconsistent.\n\nSo, the answer should be option B.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B\n\nStep-by-step explanation:\n\n1. From the given information, A < B \u2264 C, so A is definitely less than C, making A = C impossible.\n2. Therefore, option B, which states A and C have the same power consumption, must be inconsistent.\n\nAnswer: B",
