hor is challenging this hypothesis by pointing out that the prey's size would affect it, thus undermining the initial assumption.\n\nSo I think D is the correct answer.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: D\n\nThe first statement in the argument is presented as a hypothesis that the argument attempts to undermine by questioning its sufficiency as evidence. \n\nThe argument initially concludes that T. rex was a scavenger because of its size, but the author challenges this hypothesis by pointing out that the size of the prey could affect the conclusion. Therefore, the first statement is a hypothesis that the argument seeks to undermine.\n\nThe correct option is: D",
