g doesn't help. So, this could be the answer.\n\nOption D: \"Tourist explorers who illegally enter unsafe areas and waste social resources and taxpayers' money should bear the corresponding expenses.\" This supports charging because it's pointing out that these adventurers are causing waste and should pay for their actions. So, this supports the positive side, meaning it's not the answer.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the question is asking which option cannot support the positive side. Option C is the one that argues against charging by saying it doesn't help in building social responsibility, which would not support the positive side's argument. Therefore, the correct answer is C.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: C\n\nThe reasoning is that option C argues that simple charges won't help in establishing social responsibility, which contradicts the positive side's stance that charging is necessary. \n\nThe correct option is: C",
