ange is causing more tornadoes in that area. So C doesn't weaken the conclusion.\n\nOption D: Explaining that tornadoes come from thunderstorms with convection doesn't directly link climate change to more tornadoes. It just explains the mechanism. So D doesn't weaken the conclusion either.\n\nWait, but the question is which option does NOT weaken the conclusion. So all options except one either support or don't weaken it. But the question is asking which one does not weaken the conclusion, so the correct answer is the one that doesn't provide a reason to think the conclusion is wrong.\n\nSo, the correct answer is B because it supports the conclusion, meaning it doesn't weaken it. The other options either don't affect or support the conclusion, but B is the one that doesn't weaken it.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B\n\nThe reasoning is that option B supports the conclusion by stating that a warm climate is necessary for tornado formation, thus linking climate change to increased tornadoes. This strengthens the conclusion rather than weakening it.\n\nThe correct option is: B",
